    "solution": "Stay seated and lean through the fork onto the high line. Strike the condenser before the train reaches the water, then take the feather flight to the observation gallery. Turn its mirror to light the receiver: this opens the sealed home exit and removes the outgoing track. Let the frozen track thaw and the train settle in the safe western part of the lower vault. Step off the gallery and steer back left once below its edge, staying west of the two permanent corner beams. Dash the train west from its eastern face and follow its moving shadow below the missing outbound bridge. Jump and dash up at the western rail end, then walk through the open home door.",
    "nearestExisting": "F18 is the nearest cart/thaw/shadow room, and B29 sends a movable shield ahead. This switchyard adds a piloted high fork, an optical latch that physically removes the outgoing rail, access to the train’s far face after thaw, and an explicit reversal that shades the lower return.",
